From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Nov 30 18:24:30 1998
From: Cy Schubert <cschuber () uumail ! gov ! bc ! ca>
Date: Mon, 30 Nov 1998 18:24:30 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Jazz Drive Boot Device
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078728412262

I received replies from Dr. Tom Blinn (tpb@doctor.zk3.dec.com) and Tom 
Webster (webster@ssdpdc.lgb.cal.boeing.com).  Dr. Blinn stated that it 
will work, however Jazz media is not the most reliable media in the 
world, so AdvFS would not be recommended.  He also stated that it 
should boot.

Mr. Webster commented that starting with DU4.0 Digital implemented 
additional features to disklabel to protect us from ourselves.  He has 
had some luck zeroing a the label first.  Mr. Webster indicated that 
depending on the DU version, newfs may not work.

Personally, I have experience with Zip drives on my FreeBSD boxes at 
home.  I have a FreeBSD desktop here at work.  Since FreeBSD reports 
the drive's fictitious geometry I will attach the Jazz drive to FreeBSD 
first to have FreeBSD report the geometry of the drive, then use that 
information to build a disktab entry for the Jazz drive for DU.  I 
suspect that editing Jazz drive disk labels to have the same 
restrictions as other disks.

I'll post a followup once the drive has been purchased and tested.


