From tru64-unix-managers  Sat Nov 28 05:50:19 1998
From: "Robert L. McMillin" <rlm () syseca-us ! com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 1998 05:50:19 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: How to configure Jaz drive against manual eject
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078728412244

<!doctype html public "-//w3c//dtd html 4.0 transitional//en">
<html>
Duh... every now and then I actually do my own digging. After I wrote this
message to the list, I found out how to prevent user ejection of a mounted
Jaz drive: use the <tt>ddr_config</tt> command after adding an entry for
the Jaz drive, like so:
<blockquote><tt>SCSIDEVICE</tt>
<br><tt>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; #</tt>
<br><tt>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; # Entry for the SCSI Iomega Jaz drives</tt>
<br><tt>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; #</tt>
<br><tt>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Type = disk</tt>
<br><tt>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name = "iomega" "jaz"</tt>
<br><tt>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; #</tt>
<br><tt>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; PARAMETERS:</tt>
<blockquote><tt>&nbsp;TypeSubClass&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
= floppy_3.5</tt>
<br><tt>&nbsp;DynamicGeometry&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; = true</tt>
<br><tt>&nbsp;TagQueueDepth&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; = 0</tt>
<br><tt>&nbsp;CMD_PreventAllow&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; = supported</tt></blockquote>
</blockquote>
This is basically a copy of the Zip drive entry. Curiously, the entry claims
that this is a RX25 drive, but a quick search of the Businesslink database
indicates there's no such device. Does anybody know what's going on here?
Is the RX25 a figment of that author's imagination?
<p>--
