As always quick replies.

Thanks to all who answered (7 persons in just under 2 hours!).

The question was regarding preventing a disk from spinning down and it
appears there are two solutions:

1. Use 'dxpower' to customize several energy saving preferences.

2. Modify /etc/sysconfigtab and add (with 'sysconfigdb') the following
entries in stanza-format:

pwrmgr:
	cpu_slowdown=0
	disk_spindown=0

