The KZPBA-anything is not supported in any TruCluster environment.
The latest patch kit for 3.2G (I found patch kit 4) is required for proper
HSZ70 communication.
Some people seemed to prefer the route of destroying everything, starting
afresh and restoring a backup.

In the end, I can say that important things to have before you start are
     a full backup of everything
     a printout of your ASE database (I copied the db to a V4 system and
used asemgr to get a text output)
     a printout of how to manually reinstate the file domains and LSM
volumes after you've screwed up ASE and it's deleted them ;-)

We managed to migrate some data using addvol and rmvol, but having one of
the HSZ40s wired up backwards (i.e. rz20 was really rz28 etc) meant that we
lost a couple of domains and had to recover from backup.

Thanks
/tmp


