From tru64-unix-managers  Sun Nov 15 22:58:00 1998
From: Hugh Pritchard <Hugh.Pritchard () MCI ! com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 1998 22:58:00 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: netstat -an gives "no namelist"
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078728411921

Thanks to the timely responses of 
    Thomas Leitner <tom@finwds01.tu-graz.ac.at>
    Kym Schwarz <schwarz@stl.dec.com>
and especially
    "Douglas B. Jones" <douglas@gpc.peachnet.edu>
I was able to quickly find the problem: /sbin/kloadsrv was
mysteriously not running any longer!  Digital/Compaq says they've
seen this happen under high internet-connection loads.  I simply
restarted it:

    # /sbin/kloadsrv

/sbin/init.d/autosysconfig does this at boot time.

Other suggestions were to check /vmunix for being re-built (but no
reboot yet) or stripped.

My original question was,

> On one of my DU 4.0D boxes, netstat -an gives "no namelist."
> I vaguely remember this error message as being due to the misuse
> of the Fortran NAMELIST statement.  However,
> 
>     - netstat is the same as on other DU 4.0D boxes (so sayeth
>       cksum and sum), and on the other boxes netstat works;
>     - it does this under as vanilla an environment as I can make;
>     - I imagine netstat is written in C, or Alpha assembler, or
>       Bliss or somesuch, not Fortran.

