Dear managers:

	Once again I want to thank to all of you, and specially to: Mike
Plante, Nestor Ruiz, Phil Farrell, Stan Horwitz, Brian Hostetter and
Salvador Ramirez.

	My problem was I have to restrict the user's ability to change their
information (name, office, phone, etc).

	In general this were two solutions:

	- Change permissions to the chfn program, but because chfn is a hard
link to passwd, if I make this the users can't change their passwords!

	- Erase the chfn command, but if I make this users can use passwd -f
to chage their information.

	- Comment the line:
siad_chg_finger=(OSFC2,/usr/shlib/libsecurity.so) in the file
/etc/sia/matrix.conf. The only inconvenience is that no one can change
users information, not even root.

					Gil Renard


