Short summary: I have received 2 flames and 1 resume
--

I have received a couple of flames from the (I suspect self-appointed) list
police regarding the job advert I posted on this list, along the lines of:

> If you're not a subscriber to an international mailing list and don't know
> what the list policies are, it would behoove you to find out BEFORE you post
> to the list.  Doing otherwise is unethical and inconsiderate.

I absolutely agree, which is why I read the summary of the Alpha-OSF-managers
charter and rules, and also asked our outgoing SysAdmin (who was a long-term
subscriber) whether it would be appropriate, before I sent the job
announcement.

Although obviously not the primary purpose of the list, the job advertisement
is, in effect, a "Digital UNIX on Alpha systems management question", and our
outgoing SysAdmin assured me that he had seen job adverts on the list before.

However, I now realise that this was too liberal an interpretation of the
summary, for which I apologise: Rest assured, this will be my last message to
this list -- like most of you, I'm too busy to deal with spam and flame mail.

You may be interested to know, however, that I received an e-mail resume
within an hour of posting the announcement, so for at least one member of the
list, the message was very much on-topic.

Cheers,

T.
