From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Nov 10 20:28:28 1998
From: Dan Kirkpatrick <dkirk () suhep ! phy ! syr ! edu>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 1998 20:28:28 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: getty: cannot open "/dev/tty00". errno: 6
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078728411820

Thanks to "Dr. Tom Blinn, 603-884-0646" <tpb@doctor.zk3.dec.com>

Solution:
>If "console" is the same device as "/dev/tty00" which is the case when you
>boot the system using a serial console, then you can't have both lines in
>the /etc/inittab file or one of the two getty programs will ALWAYS fail and
>you will get the symptoms you see.
That did it... I had both console and /dev/tty00 lines in /etc/inittab...
I took the /dev/tty00 out and left the other... no problems now... Thanks!

