Subject: SUMMARY: ADVFS Backup/restore
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078728411738

Thanks to all who tried to help me to that problem:

Oisin McGuiness
Dr Blinn
Martin Mokrejs
Mitsch Bertone
Georg Tasman ( a comment to Georg, I can't reply to your domain db.com?)

It seems that I was producing the problem.

The rule is as follow:

the advfs domain names are allowed only once while fileset names should
reflect the targeted fileset.

This gives the following correction to my script:

/sbin/mkfset bck1_domain bck1			<<<=== wrong
/sbin/mount bck1_domain#bck1 /mnt/bck1

/sbin/mkfdmn -F -t rz28m /dev/rz1a bck1_domain
/sbin/mkfset bck1_domain root			<<<=== Right
/sbin/mount bck1_domain#root /mnt/bck1

and so forth for each other domains. Now I can plug the backup disk to the
slot of the previous disk and it works fine.


Original mail:

I'm doing backup from disk to disk to speed up the restore process on our
system. Yesterday I had the possibility to try my procedure live. And I got
a real surprise. It seems that there is somthing wrong with the way I'm
doing it.

I first use a procedure submitted by crontab:

