the=20
patch #2 of Dunix 4.0d  (duv40das00002-19980717.tar)
It seems that domains created before the #2 patch was applied
MAY run into the above problem.

The solution is simple to say , but heavy to do:

1) apply the #2 patch
2) backup all your data
3) umount each fset
4) delete each domain
5) (otional ?) =09a) scu format the SCSI disks
=09=09b) re-initialize Logical Drive for RAID SWXCR disks
6) re-create each domain and fset
7) re-mount each fset
8) restore all your data

It worked for me (up to now, at least: finger crossed!)=20
To be sure to have a clean situation I did the above point 5) but I'm
not sure it was necessary.
Since my root & usr filesystems are both AdvFs, I had to use a
secondary boot disk (which I already had) to recreate the normal root &
usr domains in the above way.

