From: Stephen Trew <s.trew () bigfoot ! com>
Date: Tue, 03 Nov 1998 09:06:00 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY pwd: Permission denied
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078728411642

Hi folks,

Thanks to Hoai Tran who hit the nail on the head with this
one.

The Problem:

> Recently we upgraded to DU 4.0 and I've got a strange
> problem.  Here it is:
>
> % pwd
> pwd: Permission denied
> %
>
> What did upgrading do so I lose access to optain a result
> from pwd and how do I fix it?

Hoai's answer:

> It is most likely caused the account you are using does
not have rx access
> the directories above the current directory.

After the upgrade /usr had permissions:

d-wx-wx--x  35 root     system      8192 Oct 29 10:47 usr

When I chmod to allow read permission it solved the problem.

Thanks also to Jeff Berliner, Sean McGlynn, Daniel Clar, &
Dr. Thomas P. Blinn

Stephen
